\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{A diagram is an object of the categorical functor object \code{Fun(J,C)}; its core is \code{MapCat(J,C)}. A chosen strict presentation may represent that diagram through a proved comparison with relative maps. Natural equivalences between diagrams are retained, including equivalences between functors with different object functions.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{Discrete source and target categories can still have nontrivial diagram cores.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rejected}
  \p{A fixed-label presheaf mapping space as the entire diagram ∞-groupoid.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Acceptance}
  \p{\ref{at-fd-0004}; the discrete functor-category comparison.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{provisional until the bootstrap \code{Fun} comparison is proved at \ref{ms-foundation}.}
}
